Derived from MRTG
-----------------

LinkScope is a modified version of MRTG, the Multi Router Traffic Grapher,
version 2.17.10:

    Copyright (C) 1995-2022 Tobias Oetiker and the MRTG contributors
    https://oss.oetiker.ch/mrtg/  ·  https://github.com/oetiker/mrtg
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

Derived from MRTG (rewritten in Rust, October 2026):

    crates/config     MRTG's configuration grammar, validation and Target
                      syntax (bin/mrtg, lib/mrtg2/MRTG_lib.pm)
    crates/rate       the .log file format, rate calculation and
                      consolidation (src/rateup.c)
    crates/linkscope  polling behaviour, the interface cache, thresholds,
                      daemon mode and cfgmaker (bin/mrtg, bin/cfgmaker)
    crates/linkscope/src/oid_table.rs, iftype_table.rs
                      OID and ifType names (lib/mrtg2/MRTG_lib.pm,
                      bin/cfgmaker)

Changes from MRTG: everything was rewritten in Rust. The Perl evaluation of
configuration was replaced by a safe expression compiler, SNMPv3 and a
built-in web UI were added, and HTML/PNG output was dropped. The full list
of differences is in docs/COMPATIBILITY.md; security changes are in
docs/SECURITY.md.

LinkScope is not affiliated with or endorsed by Tobias Oetiker or the MRTG
project. "MRTG" is used only to describe compatibility and origin.


